From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seabraid <seabraid@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/16] seabraid phase 1: --remote-expert-opt works across the
 helper process; the helper returns per-token weighted sums

seabraid_helper_begin writes each helper-owned pick's router weight into the channel weights region and asks for kOutPerToken; the helper sums w * expert(x) per token on its own card (the same RemoteExpertOpt reduce an in-process helper GPU uses) and returns n_tok rows instead of one row per pick. seabraid_helper_finish requires the echo (out_mode == kOutPerToken, out_rows == n_tok), else it is a helper error, then RemoteExpertOpt::accumulate fills h_sum_/h_mask_ exactly as for an in-process remote. Without an active RemoteExpertOpt window nothing changes (per-pick).

RemoteExpertOpt: init/destructor/adapt/owns skip or ask holds() for a helper-process remote (no GPU, no cache_ in this process); accumulate takes the rows pointer; sum_rows() for the helper; init_host_only() for CPU tests. SEABRAID_STRATA_HOT_SHARE no longer refuses --remote-expert-opt (the refusal existed because the helper could not serve it).

Test: tests/core/remote_experts_seabraid_opt_test.cpp, an in-process fake helper on a real shm channel (CPU only). Sabotaged: weight 1.0, accept wrong out_rows, accept a per-pick answer: each fails it.
